94c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit 3307 (40bbd330e17a6f11ba2049ac8b1dfdab8736c86e). Before: both parametrized interface cases (ambient origin with another URL; ambient sync.remote=upstream) accepted the write onto a no-common-ancestor tracker; the unit test failed on the missing repo_root parameter. After: new tests 3/3 pass; freshness, store-write, opcert, fsck and import modules 433 passed with 1 xdist worker crash in the 3000-ticket import benchmark that did not reproduce alone (module 5/5); make lint and make typecheck exit 0. make verify: 20764 passed, 2 failed, both the pre-existing bald-diagnostic-cricket logging-handler failures, reproduced with this change's source reverted to main.","timestamp":1793805866361205001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793776499948210001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f66d3b58-4f95-414c-b738-e5337e4bebcb","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1561-dc08-688f-49ae"},{"link_uuid":"92c566d6-8a33-49e4-b395-96ac631fddde","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2bea-e35d-eec3-4e52"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`write_blocking_divergence(tracker)` (`src/rebar/_store/freshness.py:169`) is the pre-write guard that refuses a ticket write to a tracker with no common ancestor with the fetched shared store (bug `2d52-5abe-abb8-44ab`). Its only callers pass the tracker alone: `_seam._refuse_unpublishable_store(tracker)` (`src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:391`, called from `finalize_event` at `_seam.py:386`) and the importer flush (`src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py:159`). The guard then resolves the code repo from the ambient process with `config.repo_root_or_none()` (`freshness.py:189`: `REBAR_ROOT`, else cwd), not from the write's `repo_root`.\n\nObserved 2026-11-03 while profiling the op-cert `jobs.run_job` for `upset-prissy-olm`: a completion-PASS SIGNATURE write ran `git -C <pytest REBAR_ROOT sandbox> remote get-url origin`, a repo unrelated to the write.\n\n### Root cause (reproduced)\n\n`append_event` binds an operation snapshot for the explicit `repo_root` (`_seam.py:477`). The guard passes the ambient path to `config.tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote`; `_bound_snapshot_for_root` (`src/rebar/config.py:124`) rejects the snapshot for a different root, so the branch and remote names load from the ambient repo's config. The guard then compares the ambient repo's `git remote get-url <remote>` against the tracker's (`freshness.py:194-210`) and returns `None` when they differ.\n\nSandbox repro (owner repo A with its tracker rebuilt on an orphan history, so `merge-base HEAD origin/tickets` fails; ambient repo B via `REBAR_ROOT`, whose `origin` URL differs):\n\n- ambient = A: guard returns `diverged`, `rebar.comment(..., repo_root=A)` is refused, tracker HEAD unchanged.\n- ambient = B: guard runs `get-url` in B, sees a URL mismatch, returns `None` after 2 git calls; `rebar.comment(..., repo_root=A)` commits the event onto the split history. **A real no-common-ancestor divergence is skipped and the event is stranded.**\n\nA differing `sync.remote` in the ambient repo skips the check the same way: the tracker has no such remote, so `rev-parse <remote>/<branch>` fails and the guard returns `None`.\n\n### Why the guard compares URLs\n\n`test_write_divergence_probe_ignores_repointing_tracker_remote` (`tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py:161`): a copied test fixture's tracker can still point at another origin, and the guard must not refuse on a remote-tracking ref that is not this project's shared store. The code repo's `sync.remote` URL identifies the shared store, so the comparison is only meaningful against the repo that owns the write. That intent is preserved.\n\n## Approach\n\nFollow the existing write-path resolution: the config-way code root, honoring an explicit root. `_remote_ref` (`freshness.py:55`) and `fsck_tracker_health._tracker_sync_status` (`src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py:151`) resolve `tickets.remote`/`tickets.branch` from `config.repo_root_or_none()`, not from the tracker's parent, because `rebar.toml` lives in the checkout. `repo_root_or_none(explicit)` (`src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:225`) already takes an explicit root first. The write path already carries that root: all 8 `finalize_event` call sites pass `repo_root`, and `import_tickets` holds it as `rr` (`import_ndjson.py:109`).\n\n1. `write_blocking_divergence(tracker=None, *, repo_root=None)`: resolve `base = config.repo_root_or_none(repo_root)` and default the tracker with `config.tracker_dir(repo_root)`. `repo_root=None` keeps today's ambient behavior for callers that pass neither.\n2. `_refuse_unpublishable_store(tracker, repo_root=None)` forwards it; `finalize_event` passes its `repo_root`.\n3. `import_ndjson._flush` passes `repo_root=rr`.\n4. Update the importer test's fake (`tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py:73`) to accept the new keyword.\n\nNo new mechanism (no config key, env var, lock or fixture). The read-only gate reads (`store_freshness`, `_remote_ref`) are out of scope: they take no `repo_root`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/freshness.py` — `write_blocking_divergence` takes and uses `repo_root`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py` — thread `repo_root` through `finalize_event` → `_refuse_unpublishable_store`.\n- `src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py` — pass `repo_root=rr` at the flush.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py` — new failing-first regression tests.\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py` — unit test that the guard's git calls use the explicit repo.\n- `tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py` — fake accepts `repo_root`.\n\n## Testing\n\nFailing tests first, no autouse fixtures, child processes started with `tests._subprocess_env.subprocess_env`.\n\n- Interface, parametrized over 2 ambient repos (same `sync.remote` name with a different URL; a different `sync.remote` in `rebar.toml`): the owner tracker has no common ancestor with `origin/tickets`, `REBAR_ROOT` points at the ambient repo, and `rebar.comment(seed, ..., repo_root=owner)` must raise `RebarError` containing `ticket write refused` with tracker HEAD unchanged. Both fail on current main (the write is accepted).\n- Unit: `write_blocking_divergence(tracker, repo_root=owner)` with `REBAR_ROOT` at another repo records every `run_git` cwd; none is the ambient repo, and the remote probed is the owner's `sync.remote`.\n- Edge: `repo_root=None` keeps the ambient resolution; the existing remote-mismatch and non-store-ref unit tests and `test_first_write_refuses_unrelated_diverged_store` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A test writes a ticket event with an explicit `repo_root` while `REBAR_ROOT` points at a different repo whose `sync.remote` differs. It asserts that `write_blocking_divergence` reads the explicit repo's remote, and no git process runs against the ambient repo.\n- [x] A sandbox test whose owner tracker has no common ancestor with its fetched `origin/tickets`, run with `REBAR_ROOT` at an unrelated repo, shows the write refused (`ticket write refused`) and tracker HEAD unchanged. It fails on the pre-fix code.\n- [x] The existing divergence-refusal tests pass unchanged: `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py` exits 0.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0 with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on `PATH`.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The change merges through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n  provenance: environment=Gerrit rebar.solutions.navateam.com project rebar, change 3307; principal=RebarBotNava (Contributors submitter; votes cast by the review-bot and CI); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — GET /a/changes/3307 with DETAILED_LABELS on 2026-11-04 showed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 (CI run 41866404033) on revision 40bbd330e17, revision-scoped submit returned MERGED as 1c8a67702f8, and that SHA is an ancestor of origin/main.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/freshness.py","reason":"write_blocking_divergence resolves the code repo from an explicit repo_root"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","reason":"thread repo_root from finalize_event into _refuse_unpublishable_store"},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","reason":"importer flush passes its repo_root to the guard"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py","reason":"regression: divergence refused when REBAR_ROOT is an unrelated repo"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py","reason":"unit: guard git calls run against the explicit repo only"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py","reason":"importer fake accepts the repo_root keyword"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2bea-e35d-eec3-4e52"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7abdfa31-1655-4036-afdb-5b81cd206d79","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1a62-acd6-6ab7-4152","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Write divergence guard reads the ambient repo, not the tracker's","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c4817762-ee7b-489e-b694-f5e1da141335","6f51f805-04fa-4f50-a2c0-aa0bdb023d9e","175838e9-8fbe-4ad8-bf73-0060bf9f1c17","aa4f4e98-9a99-4d2e-b2f7-2cc99aed4cda","373f6861-5503-486d-8